{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512431-do-you-use-magical-items-artifacts-in-your-games","id":1512431,"title":"Do you use magical items/artifacts in your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-23T05:37:12-07:00","id":1512431,"title":"Do you use magical items/artifacts in your games?","content":"Unlike other RPGs including other WoD games, Vampire, with the notable exclusion of bloodlines, isn't heavy on magic items. Hunters Hunted has relics to be used in the context of vampire, but the expected vampire exploitation of such relics hasn't been mentioned despite the great potential of vampires to accumulate such things. Thaumaturges have a handful of permanent items like the vessel of transference or Wards (a fantastic family of spells) Mirror Prisons, and can, if they're willing to invest four levels into a relatively obscure path, fetishes, although vampire fetishes are burdened with absolute bullshit like &quot;Fetishes created by this power are often unreliable and fail at inopportune moments, as the spirits within are understandably displeased with their situation and will take any opportunity to escape or thwart their captors.&quot;, and werewolves will apparently frenzy at seeing a vampire fetish regardless of what kind of spirit you've trapped in there, at least in <i>Rites of the Blood</i>. I am very fond of malfean factories and weird stuff like banewhips, which aren't true fetishes, and I can imagine some trade going on in that direction.<br /> Probably, Vampires could use kinfolk fetishes as they don't require gnosis, and perhaps demon/ghost possessed items could have some power. Vamps probably wouldn't recognized something enchanted by changelings.<br /> <br /> Mages... in theory, there could be great parnerships between vampires and mages. Due to political realities, it's unlikely to blossom into anything positive, but there are some room for repurposements. Vampires look at mages and see cool toys, mages look at vampires and see... ingredients (to be fair, some vampires look at other vampires that way)<br /> <br /> whether it's actually useful items or unknowable McGuffins to sell to the Tremere, how do y'all see things?<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T06:11:58-07:00","id":1512438,"title":"","content":"Usually with the Settite magical items made by Akhu ritual, like<br /> <b>Dreams of Duat</b>: The Setite needs parts of the victim's body. Sealing them in a wax figure, the lector-priest inscribes the victim's name in hieroglyphic script on it. Cursing the target, the lector-priest washes the figurine in warm water made bitter with natron. The victim will have nightmares about Duat in the following night.<br /> <b>Scorpion Sending:</b> The Lector-Priest sculpts a scorpion out of wax, incorporating small parts of the intended victim's body, like hair, nail clippings, and similar, into it. After writing Set's name on the back of the scorpion in green ink and reciting the tale of Horus' poisoning, the Lector-Priest has to carry the figurine to a place frequented by the victim. When the target comes near the figurine, it will transform into a real scorpion and sting him.<br /> <b>Severing Sands: </b>The Lector-Priest gathers authentic sand from the Nile bank, washed clean and dried in the sun. Sprinkling the sand with perfumes, natron, and his own vitae, he recites a prayer to the life-giving Nile. When confronted by a supernatural creature, the Setite may blow the sand against them with a prayer to the respective god (Seker for vampires, Anubis for wraiths, Set for demons etc.). Incorporeal creatures are banished back into their home realms, while other supernaturals lose their healing powers.<br /> <b>Summon Sebau: </b>The Lector-Priest constructs a clay model mixed with vitae of one of the Sebau to command it. If the Lector-Priest wants the Sebau to attack a target, he needs a piece of its body or its True Name.<br /> <br /> And of course, even to use the <b>Path of Duat</b>, the Magician must carry a talismanic gem of black onyx carved with the image of a mummified man - the form of Sokar, the god of Duat. A few minutes before using the path, the magician smears the talisman with a drop of her own blood as an offering to Sokar, and whispers a short prayer. The hypnotic aspects of the Path of Duat mean that all powers operate at a +1 difficulty if the lector-priest does not catch the victim's attention using the darkly glittering talisman on the turn when she initiates the magic. <br /> - So in a sense, the little amulet of Seker is a magic item<br /> <br /> Aside the Akhu, stuff made with Koldunic rituals also could be considered &quot;magical items/artifacts&quot; in my humble opinion<br /> <br /> In the Spear of Bethel thread we listed a tons of vampiric artifacts, and some of them seen a lot of usage in my games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T06:15:58-07:00","id":1512440,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say common, but most of my longer running chronicles end up with a magical doodad or two being introduced at some point. Eventually some is going to show up with an enchanted cane or pocketwatch or knife, especially if the Tremere, Followers of Set or other magical focused clan play a big role. That doesn't mean the magical doodad will play a role in the campaign, or even that the players will necessarily know that NPC X has a magic knife, but it'll be there in the background if it becomes relevant.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Fetishes created via Spirit Manipulation, as a house rule I tend to rule that Fetishes created with banes or Wyrm spirits are generally okay with being controlled by a vampire, provided the vampire offers one point of vitae (it doesn't have to be his own) per week as a sort of payment for services. In such a case, the fetish won't break or malfunction, though of course the vampire (and his magical tool) will very much reek of the Wyrm. These tend to be relatively common among the Followers of Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-23-2023, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T07:12:26-07:00","id":1512450,"title":"","content":"I don't really use them unless something specifically occult is happening or I want to throw the city into chaos by throwing in a powerful magic item and watching everyone kill each other over it. They're rare, and often require an understanding of what they are and how to use them.<br /> <br /> Ritual objects are the most commonly seen. Fetters, &quot;devil sticks&quot;, blasphemy shrines, <i>shabti</i>, warding objects, vials powering the Domino of Life, etc. I'd have it that items (even mundane ones) that are used frequently in rituals begin to reduce the difficulty or add bonus die or have other strange side effects.<br /> <br /> I also have a personal favourite category of magic &quot;items&quot; that involves strange looking statues and idols and things that are actually perfectly aware, still powerful and still scheming vampires forced into fancy new shapes (like that Koldun from<i> Rites of the Blood</i> who likes turning his fellow kindred blood sorcerers into explanatory text books that teach you new paradigms). Sometimes they can still use their disciplines, make the right deal and they might use them on your behalf a few times while they're plotting to use you to free and avenge themselves of this humiliation.<br /> <br /> Then there's stuff like holy relics like Buddhist <i>\u015bar\u012bras</i> or the nails from the Crucifixion; usually the opposite of helpful to a vampire, since I'd probably give such objects True Faith ratings (unless we're going for a &quot;cleanse me of the curse&quot; type game), but if you desecrated them in some fashion they could probably pull of some interesting ritual effects.<br /> Or from vampiric faiths, so something or other used by Set, something from Caine's journeys at the dawn of time, a clipping from Lilith's garden... likely to have interesting benefits and side effects to the holder, and useful in rituals, but I'd probably use them more like plot hooks with visions and omens and such.<br /> <br /> <br /> For cross-splat objects, Quintessence, Gnosis, Glamour, Pathos, Qi and Vitae and anything else are exactly the same things in different format, it's simply a matter of knowing how to translate. So fetishes, chimera, wonders, relics/artifacts and so forth are technically usable to the kindred, but they need to have at least a basic understanding of the other splat and a &quot;translation&quot; ability - and possibly an ally or allies from the other side of the equation. You need to be a necromancer to make any use out of WtO's stuff, have a grasp of Chimestry and Ravnos lore for CtD's, etc. Those two in particular aren't of much interest to the other clans anyway, since there's nothing in the Underworld or the Dreaming that would interest the common vampire (as far as they know.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">I actually made a magical item that allowed one of my necromancers to use some of the arcanoi by himself over on the other side of the Shroud. It involved a hell of a lot of risk, jumping through hoops to find and get the assistance of wraiths with the requisite abilities (some of which are illegal under Stygian law), and the expenditure of a ridiculous amount of time, vitae, willpower and pathos to make... The result only has a limited amount of uses before it needs &quot;recharging,&quot; so it's not something used cheaply.<br /> But it did come in useful. Being able to spot when a wraith is under the control of its shadow, stepping across the shroud and teleporting to another location, time manipulation, divination, spatial distortion, essentially being able to use dominate while ignoring generation, being able to know the deepest desires of those around you (and then erase or edit them to your liking), making things decay, crafting illusions...\u200b</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T08:19:34-07:00","id":1512455,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> I mostly play and run Dark Ages, so it comes more easily. But yeah, I love supernatural items, especially those drawing upon real-world legends.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I wrote a Storytellers Vault book with, among other things, magical items for Dark Ages and I am planning on doing a book for modern day with legendary items of the clans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T09:20:49-07:00","id":1512463,"title":"","content":"We haven't used them all that much in our games as we felt that the disciplines were more then enough in most situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T09:42:37-07:00","id":1512466,"title":"","content":"Magic items and Vampires are always a strange combination.<br /> <br /> Thanks to an unlimited lifespan a vampire can become insanely wealthy, which means for a magical item to have value it would have to do something that can't be replicated by spending money or using a discipline that the cainite picked up along the way. But the only things a vampire would generally want that can't be replicated by money or disciplines is something that cancels vampiric weaknesses, but that breaks the game. Such as the rings from the Vampire Diaries that protect vampires from sunlight and allow day walking.<br /> <br /> The Kindred of the East game line of V:tM has quite a few magical items as well as rituals for creating them, so they are not just artifacts from a long-lost civilization. But this tends to not break the game because the KotE line was designed to be a cross over native setting, rather than a stand-alone which can be crossed over. So, a Kuei-jin might be rich in the real world, but the instant they go into the umbra or one of the hells, they need other equipment or resources. Despite being one of the last game lines developed, KotE was more of a pick and mix of other systems. Specifically, the fetish crafting system from Werewolf was used as the basis.<br /> <br /> So, you could get things like a player who binds a spirit with say 10 soak dice into an amulet, which they can activate for a scene to gain those soak dice, but since the character had rank five Iron Mountain for their Demon power, that means they are now soaking all non-agg damage with 15 soak dice at difficulty 2 and one auto success. Then add actual body armor and a max survivability build with Demon Shintai and yeah the ST will be hard pressed to do meaningful damage.<br /> <br /> Vampire was originally designed to be street level with characters that wouldn't look out of place with the Lost Boys vampires. Magical items are usually plot items the PCs chase after but never get to keep. Personally I have no issue with using magical items in Vampire games but you have to consider how all the other vampires would behave if magical items were either widely available or if they were rare, that they could cover important weaknesses.<br /> <br /> As for Mages, magical items, and Vampires... once again that gets tricky because there is a whole other area of ramifications that needs to be considered. Officially there is a specific combination of sphere ratings that would allow a mage to cure vampirism in a character and turn them back into a normal human. But if a Mage with the right sphere ratings can erase the curse of Caine, then theoretically they should be able to enhance it. Why build a magical item for a vampire when you can artificially induce Golconda which unlocks stat &amp; discipline limits and locks down the beast. Even if you don't use the Golconda as a short hand, there are plenty of adjustments that can be made.<br /> <br /> In the end magical items will always turn a game into a gear check, rather than a character build check or a role play check. Think of your favorite MMO and think of Vampires as max ranked characters but without any gear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T10:51:20-07:00","id":1512474,"title":"","content":"They had the same type of ring that protected vampires from the sun and being staked in Buffy &amp; Angel that was promptly destroyed by Angel as he felt he wasn't worthy of such a gift If I remember correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T11:30:43-07:00","id":1512479,"title":"","content":"I have a very liberal view on splat exclusivity regarding sorcery, so I would have absolutely no problem with converting the mortal Enchantment path to blood sorcery. Honestly, most of what runs under the blood sorcery label doesn't even make sense as magic that needs vitae to function. IIRC, one of the older books even mentions this as an option and I think there is a Thauma path that lets you create new paths in character.<br /> But even without dedicated path, I think it's not unreasonable to assume someone proficient in rituals could create a few minor items, even if it's just for narrative flavor. A wangateur with an enchanted skull is simply more fun than without one, as is the Tremere with Auspex 1 glasses.<br /> <br /> It may be different for Dark Ages games, but I think lesser magical gadgets are mostly absent from Vampire because they can easily create tonal dissonance with the setting. For Werewolves and Mages they are anchored in the culture of the respective splat, while for vampires they are tools for a minority. The utility of many lesser items can also be emulated with modern technology, and that is a lot more easily available if you have money.<br /> <br /> It didn't come up for me so far, but I would probably ignore most restrictions on Spirit Thauma fetishes. Vampires forcing spirits into service is too on brand than to spoil it with bad guy demerits.<br /> <br /> I think an interesting twist for vampire enchanting could be the use of cursed objects, since it's thematically fitting. Maybe something that resonates with Caine's curse and lets vampires bypass or redirect the effect of hexed objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T15:22:27-07:00","id":1512495,"title":"","content":"I have, but they've mostly tended to be fairly unique items in the vein (npi) of those in the original Sabbat book (Talbot's Chainsaw, Aaron's Feeding Razor, etc.) that were as much the result of happenstance as anything else. But sometimes also more common oddities made using blood sorcery rituals. (IIRC, the original Vampire Storytellers Handbook had several listed in the back appendix.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T17:31:40-07:00","id":1512508,"title":"","content":"I've never actually used any magical items in the chronicles I have been the ST. I do not object to them in principal, but if I do ever introduce them I would want them to be few in number, appropriate for the genre, and actually drive some kind of plot. I don't want magic items just to be magic items, and would very much want to avoid any inclination or feel that this is something like a D&amp;D scenario.<br /> <br /> So they could not be generic or mass produced. Each one would need its own kind of legendary history and lore behind it. They would not actually be all that powerful, though they would be useful in some kind of capacity. I would probably also want them to be legacies of an earlier age when magic was more present in the world, and there are less and less of them every year simply because of attrition (though some may also just stop working because the world is just becoming more inhospitable to them - at least until Gehenna begins). Each historical era has its own sweet spot in terms of how much magic should exist.<br /> <br /> There would also be some slight amount of crossover as there should be competition over control of these resources. Introduce a magical item, and it should not just be something that vampires fight over, but would attract the attention of Lupines, Bastet, Mages, Sorcerers, hunters, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T23:34:08-07:00","id":1512545,"title":"","content":"I mean RAW a fetish created with Spirit Manipulation is also going to fail, if you botch a Willpower roll against the fetishes level+3 when activating it. That's not going to happen that often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T00:32:59-07:00","id":1512548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512431-do-you-use-magical-items-artifacts-in-your-games?p=1512545#post1512545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean RAW a fetish created with Spirit Manipulation is also going to fail, if you botch a Willpower roll against the fetishes level+3 when activating it. That's not going to happen that often.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's completely fine because it's RAW and dealt entirely with mechanics. But entirely separate is the idea that fetishes will fail at inopportune times... you don't give the storyteller that kind of loaded gun. <br /> <i>Player&quot; Oh I'm in a precarious situation, my fetish is good for this scenario so I roll willpower and... <br /> Storyteller: Nah your fetish decides now is the time to rebel, because it's smart and is watching you and knows this is the best time, and also because the other players are jealous and I really hate that you made four of these things and have a great option for every scenario without having to have spent so much xp on them. <br /> Player: Oh Ok I'm just going to go ahead and die then. Next character will start with 5 resources and tons of other great backgrounds out of petty revenge. </i><br /> <br /> Spirit manipulation is a shitty path. It's written with so many vague caveats that make it much worse than Presence. A generous GM might make it OP and have it super easy to get incorporeal spirits to effect the world ,while others will make it nigh impossible to enlist umbral help. 1 is virtually useless on it's own. 2 seems sabotaged by the writers because the concept seems good but there are so many strings dragging things down, 3 is the same, 4 is actually really great <i>so long as your storyteller isn't ever a dick</i>. and 5 is more dangerous than it is useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T00:47:43-07:00","id":1512549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512431-do-you-use-magical-items-artifacts-in-your-games?p=1512548#post1512548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's completely fine because it's RAW and dealt entirely with mechanics. But entirely separate is the idea that fetishes will fail at inopportune times... you don't give the storyteller that kind of loaded gun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would interpret that the part with the Willpower roll as the mechanical implementation of the fluff text, but I guess not every GM is going to see it that way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T07:56:59-07:00","id":1512574,"title":"","content":"So how do people feel about vampire characters wanting to use hunter relics, either from spoils of war or character creation?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it's fine, though vampires are greedy and covetous and seeing holy auras, will try underhanded methods to obtain such things, and so owners must either be incredibly powerful or keep their item secret. The kind of organizations that have these things do not take their loss to undead kindly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T08:49:05-07:00","id":1512581,"title":"","content":"I'm sure if a Vampire could get its hand on such stuff (like a collector, or like Becket, or a Kiasyd relic hunter... or basically any vampire) would either use it if culd figure out how to do it, or would stash it away untill find someone who could us it (and be a usefull pawn) - or just stash it away Ark of the Covenant style, so no one could use it against the said vampire<br /> Some Baali probably would find it delightfull to taint, defile or corrupt some holy relic... or a Salubri would use it since the Warriors already share the Name of an Angel, or even a devout Cappadocian<br /> The Followers of Set were collectors (*cough* Fire Court *cough*), like of Hesha would even seek them as a profession<br /> So yeah, I would allow it if my players would ever want to persue such prize...<br /> ...and face the consequnces, because oh boy, the Hunters would probably would want it back (like the Magi if a vampire would manage to snach a grimoire, codex, relic, or anything from them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T08:59:27-07:00","id":1512584,"title":"","content":"I have the vague blueprints of a game involving letting a neonate coterie killing (or finding the dead bodies of) a hunter cell and helping themselves to a lot of magic goodies that are both great fun to play with, using them to get the upper hand on their elders and climb the ranks... while drawing danger to them lie flies as various vampire occultists, aforementioned extremely annoyed elders, envious neonates, power hungry idiots, the dead hunters' friends and the dead hunters' rivals/enemies all decide they'd quite those toys themselves. For bonus points, if they're doing well enough, I'll throw in the Garou's Claw and then throw in a werewolf pack after it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T10:41:20-07:00","id":1512601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512431-do-you-use-magical-items-artifacts-in-your-games?p=1512574#post1512574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how do people feel about vampire characters wanting to use hunter relics, either from spoils of war or character creation?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it's fine, though vampires are greedy and covetous and seeing holy auras, will try underhanded methods to obtain such things, and so owners must either be incredibly powerful or keep their item secret. The kind of organizations that have these things do not take their loss to undead kindly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no problem with most of the low end stuff. I'm generally not a fan of generic &quot;Attribute/Skill +X&quot; artifacts because I think they are boring, so as player and ST I lean more towards artifacts with utility effect, preferably ones that closes a gap in a character build.<br /> For artifacts with inherit True Faith effect I would want to talk to the player if they are sure about playing around with a chunk of vampire kryptonite. I can see <i>some </i>scenarios that could make sense, but mostly I would consider even low tier holy relics too annoying to lug around.<br /> <br /> As a plot device, relic hunts are really fun though. You can send your players pretty much anywhere you like with a simple incentive and basically go full Indiana Jones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I dropped the Sword of Nul in the Mediterranean, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T16:07:17-07:00","id":1512787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512431-do-you-use-magical-items-artifacts-in-your-games#post1512431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages... in theory, there could be great parnerships between vampires and mages. Due to political realities, it's unlikely to blossom into anything positive, but there are some room for repurposements. Vampires look at mages and see cool toys, mages look at vampires and see... ingredients (to be fair, some vampires look at other vampires that way)<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>IIn many World of Darkness books and supplements I have read that the possibility and chance of good, normal, and reasonable meetings, trades, dealings, exchanges, dealings, and interactions between Vampires and Mages does distinctly exist. This type of choice / decision is definitely clear, unique, and normal.<br /> <br /> Vampires ( whether Vampires in general and overall meaning and sense, or Kindred - also known as Cainites - in particular ) and Mages - including Nephandi Mages and for example the NWO or Progenitor Technomancers and Technocrats - can definitely treat and consider each other ( and share experiences, concepts, and ideas ) as fellows, partners, lovers, friends, supporters, and allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}